// Unsafe operation checker & compile-time concurrency / data-race verifier (SPEC-30 §4, §6, §7).
// Port of bootstrap/axiom0/src/own/unsafe/unsafe.h and unsafe.c, extended in T402 with:
//   - Concurrent READ/READ sharing check (`view<T>` across threads/scopes requires `T: Share` -> `AX_CONC_VIEW_NOT_SHARE`).
//   - Concurrent READ/WRITE and WRITE/WRITE region conflict verifier (`AX_CONC_SHARED_MUT`), permitting provably
//     disjoint struct fields (`p.a` vs `p.b`) and disjoint slice sub-ranges (`v[0..2]` vs `v[2..4]`, `v[..mid]` vs `v[mid..]`),
//     while rejecting `EQUAL`, `OVERLAP`, and `UNKNOWN` region relations (`ACONCUR-150..153, 176`).
//   - Global mutable static memory check outside `unsafe` unless synchronized (`Mutex`, `RwLock`, `Atomic`) (`AX_CONC_UNSYNC_STATIC`),
//     and re-entry verification when safe `view` / `mut_view` capabilities are re-established from `unsafe` (`ACONCUR-177..178`).
//   - Synchronization lock guard escape check (`MutexGuard`, `RwLockReadGuard`, `RwLockWriteGuard`) (`AX_CONC_GUARD_ESCAPE`).
//   - Atomic non-atomic `mut_view` aliasing check (`AX_CONC_ATOMIC_MUT_VIEW`).
